<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Type "abc" into the daterangebox begin input and blur. Do the same with the
			end input, and with the datebox beside it.

		- Expected: every one of them names the pattern the user has to type —
			"You must specify a date. Format: yyyy/MM/dd" — which is what the datebox
			already says (WCAG 2.1 SC 3.3.3 Error Suggestion).
		- Bug: the daterangebox reports "Invalid range" instead. It says nothing about
			the format, and it is the same text a violated range rule gets, so a typo
			and a wrong range are indistinguishable.

		2. In the second daterangebox (minNights=2, maxNights=5), type a pair that
			PARSES but breaks a rule: 2026/09/05 then 2026/09/01, or 2026/09/01 then
			2026/09/02, or 2026/09/01 then 2026/09/20.

		- Expected, and NOT changed by this ticket: each keeps its own reason —
			"Begin date must not be later than end date", "At least 2 night(s)",
			"At most 5 night(s)". Only the parse failure above stops saying
			"Invalid range".

		3. Type "abc" into the first daterangebox begin input and blur, then click
			"change format".

		- Expected: the errorbox now says "Format: yyyy-MM-dd", the pattern the box
			parses from now on, not the one it replaced.

		Guards, each starting from "abc" in the first begin input. A redraw is
		zk.Widget.$('$drb').rerender() in the browser console.
		- Close the errorbox with its X, then "change format": it stays closed.
		- "server wrong value", then "change format": the errorbox keeps the server's
			reason.
		- "server wrong value", "server clear", then a redraw and a click into begin: the
			errorbox names the format again, not the reason the server withdrew.
		- A redraw neither reopens the errorbox nor announces it again; clicking into an input
			brings it back, unless it was closed with its X.
		- "show time off" sends the same pattern again: the errorbox must not close and
			reopen.
		Without "abc":
		- "server reject", then "change format": the server's errorbox and red border stay.
		- Type "2026-08-07" and blur, then "change format": the text now parses, so the
			errorbox closes.
	</label>
	<div>
		<button id="btnFormat" label="change format"
			onClick='drb.setFormat("yyyy-MM-dd")'/>
		<button id="btnShowTime" label="show time off"
			onClick='drb.setShowTime(false)'/>
		<button id="btnReject" label="server reject"
			onClick='drb.setEndValue(new java.util.Date(126, 7, 1)); drb.setBeginValue(new java.util.Date(126, 7, 20))'/>
		<button id="btnWrongValue" label="server wrong value"
			onClick='org.zkoss.zk.ui.util.Clients.wrongValue(drb, "Outside the booking window")'/>
		<button id="btnClear" label="server clear"
			onClick='org.zkoss.zk.ui.util.Clients.clearWrongValue(drb)'/>
	</div>
	<div>
		<daterangebox id="drb" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
			onError='lblError.setValue(event.getMessage())'/>
	</div>
	<div>
		<datebox id="db" format="yyyy/MM/dd"/>
	</div>
	<div>
		<daterangebox id="drbNights" format="yyyy/MM/dd" minNights="2" maxNights="5"/>
	</div>
	<label id="lblError" value=""/>
	<button id="btnNullReason" label="server null reason"
		onClick='org.zkoss.zk.ui.util.Clients.wrongValue(drb, (String) null)'/>
</zk>
